d Module (CM) lithium hydroxide canisters to purge carbon dioxide from the LM.", "raw": "img/AS13-62-8929.raw.jpg", "ours": "img/AS13-62-8929.ours.jpg", "nasa": "img/AS13-62-8929.nasa.jpg", "thumb": "img/AS13-62-8929.t.jpg"}, {"id": "AS13-60-8659", "mission": "13", "caption": "Excellent view of the lunar farside showing the crater Tsiolkovsky, as photographed by the crew of the Apollo 13 mission during their lunar pass.", "raw": "img/AS13-60-8659.raw.jpg", "ours": "img/AS13-60-8659.ours.jpg", "nasa": "img/AS13-60-8659.nasa.jpg", "thumb": "img/AS13-60-8659.t.jpg"}, {"id": "AS14-67-09367", "mission": "14", "caption": "", "raw": "img/AS14-67-09367.raw.jpg", "ours": "img/AS14-67-09367.ours.jpg", "nasa": "img/AS14-67-09367.nasa.jpg", "thumb": "img/AS14-67-09367.t.jpg"}, {"id": "AS14-66-09325", "mission": "14", "caption": "The third United States flag to be deployed on the lunar surface, footprints, wheel tracks and the \"Rickshaw\"-type portable workbench, as seen by the two moon-exploring astronauts from inside the Lunar Module (LM), give evidence of a busy\u2026", "raw": "img/AS14-66-09325.raw.jpg", "ours": "img/AS14-66-09325.ours.jpg", "nasa": "img/AS14-66-09325.nasa.jpg", "thumb": "img/AS14-66-09325.t.jpg"}, {"id": "AS14-66-09244", "mission": "14", "caption": "An excellent view of the lunar terrain looking through the right window of the Lunar Module (LM), photographed by one of the Apollo 14 astronauts during their stay on the lunar surface.", "raw": "img/AS14-66-09244.raw.jpg", "ours": "img/AS14-66-09244.ours.jpg", "nasa": "img/AS14-66-09244.nasa.jpg", "thumb": "img/AS14-66-09244.t.jpg"}, {"id": "AS15-82-11168", "mission": "15", "caption": "Astronaut James B. Irwin, lunar module pilot, walks away from the Lunar Roving Vehicle (LRV) during the third Apollo 15 lunar surface extravehicular activity (EVA) at the Hadley-Apennine landing site.", "raw": "img/AS15-82-11168.raw.jpg", "ours": "img/AS15-82-11168.ours3.jpg", "nasa": "img/AS15-82-11168.nasa.jpg", "before": "img